auth {
  mode: none
}

headers {
  Accept: application/json
}

docs {
  # @minerva/api

  Every request in this collection targets `apps/backend/api` — the NestJS service that the
  frontends call. The health routes come from `src/health/controller/health.controller.ts`
  and the job route from `src/app.controller.ts`; the `EmailJob` payload comes from
  `@minerva/typescript-lib` (`shared/typescript-lib/src/queue.ts`). The same routes are
  browsable as Swagger UI at `{{baseUrl}}/docs`.

  Select the **local** environment before sending anything — `{{baseUrl}}` is defined
  there, not here.

  `Accept: application/json` below covers every JSON route. `GET /health/ping` answers
  `text/plain` and overrides it on the request itself.

  The service has no authentication yet, so the collection-level auth mode is `none` and
  every request inherits it. When auth arrives, set it once here rather than per request.
}
